WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.642
The takeaway: one normalizing flow can replace a toolbox.

00:00:03.722 --> 00:00:10.499
Built on positive-definite matrices and conditioned
on both the shrinkage strength and the norm exponent,

00:00:10.579 --> 00:00:15.005
it delivers Bayesian posteriors,
marginal-likelihood model selection,

00:00:15.085 --> 00:00:19.706
and the frequentist solution path, for every
setting and every l-q norm,

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:23.298
including the non-convex sub-l-one region others avoid.

00:00:23.378 --> 00:00:26.106
Edge recovery improves where it is hardest,

00:00:26.186 --> 00:00:29.632
and sampling runs hundreds of times faster than Gibbs.
